\":0,\"year\":2025,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.4065217391304348,\"_genreOverlap\":1}],\"seasonNumber\":14,\"seasonName\":\"Series 14\",\"seasonOverview\":\"\",\"seasonPoster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/pE0ToeQbYpMChYGmB6gEhuJq61H.jpg\",\"seasonAirDate\":\"2023-05-15\",\"episodes\":[{\"number\":1,\"name\":\"Episode 1\",\"overview\":\"Upcycling supremo Sarah Moore visits Scotland's east coast, with the aim of bagging three things that can be rejuvenated and sold on for a profit.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/cprFCtGnrdicKxdIwPrv27tKLuE.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-05-15\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"Episode 2\",\"overview\":\"Upcycling aficionado Jacqui Joseph is in Beaconsfield, scouring the recycling centre for items that can be given a new lease of life rather than ending up in the skips.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/2nw9ZfWdgckXrxF8iRaO97bLFNN.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-05-17\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"Episode 3\",\"overview\":\"Sarah Moore explores Beaconsfield recycling centre, determined to save quality items from being crushed.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/y3AiOnBT9S7LEV90V8k9FqGKRfV.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-05-18\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":4,\"name\":\"Episode 4\",\"overview\":\"In East Lothian, blacksmith Kev Paxton works on some metal railings, upcycler Nicky Cash gets creative with a writing bureau, and JJ Chalmers repurposes a collection of marbles.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/7HGaoz33ns8OPM4H9TCHZUbpnnA.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-05-22\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"Episode 5\",\"overview\":\"Sarah Moore is at Witley recycling centre in Surrey, hoping to breathe new life into an Edwardian armchair, a dated display cabinet and a costume jewellery collection.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/fA5vgleS9DFSX1RoClWOgpgqYdn.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-05-24\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"Episode 6\",\"overview\":\"In Beaconsfield, carpenter Martin Hough works on a pine chest of drawers, upcycler Sarah Peterson has a trio of utility chairs, and Sarah Moore tackles a set of trestle table bases.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/4svPdn2ogbVfRHoHr84CzUFdKOX.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-05-25\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":7,\"name\":\"Episode 7\",\"overview\":\"Jacqui Joseph and the team rescue three items in Altrincham – a pair of chairs, garden cast-offs and a chest of drawers – and attempt to upcycle them into something special.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/6AaNnFz8tWCzWZBn0wLgGZfgJ0s.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-05-30\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":8,\"name\":\"Episode 8\",\"overview\":\"Sarah Moore and the team get to work on upcycling a dressing table, four glass lampshades and a dead shrub, all rescued from Keynsham recycling centre in Somerset.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/hBb8y2sjq6gSVJrVBEzItOQFWp9.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-05-31\",\"runtime\":44},{\"number\":9,\"name\":\"Episode 9\",\"overview\":\"JJ Chalmers visits Wallyford recycling centre, where he hopes to rescue some rusty saws, an unwanted dressing table and mirror, and a wooden playhouse that's in bits and pieces.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/cQvza3S6V3Ywer0euftWAUytwHW.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-06-01\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":10,\"name\":\"Episode 10\",\"overview\":\"Jacqui Joseph rescues an old, rusty pulley, a nursing chair and a table with cast-iron legs from Altrincham recycling centre.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/iQo91kSYGUyMw32a0ttlJBSV1Zy.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-06-05\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":11,\"name\":\"Episode 11\",\"overview\":\"Jacqui Joseph and her colleagues aim to bring new life to three finds in Altrincham – a four-piece coffee table set, a three-seater sofa and a pair of mid-20th-century deckchairs.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/572CXa6L9B4MANFIm1IOqiWVjuX.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-06-06\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":12,\"name\":\"Episode 12\",\"overview\":\"Sarah Moore and her team of experts get to work on upcycling a pair of mirrors, a lacrosse stick, a wrought-iron stand and a reproduction desk, all found in Beaconsfield.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/plbDMmdxu908tvjVwED3HiqdxDo.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-06-08\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":13,\"name\":\"Episode 13\",\"overview\":\"JJ Chalmers is on the lookout for quality discarded items at Wallyford recycling centre in East Lothian, hoping to bag three things that can be rejuvenated and sold on for cash.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/uHGT7Y1cqHvIEpJsSEdk3bR5TxV.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-06-12\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":14,\"name\":\"Episode 14\",\"overview\":\"Sarah Moore finds a drinks trolley, a wind-up gramophone and a collection of lampshades at Witley recycling centre to upcycle and turn into a profit.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/m59aT4YvGtEiY7E1CNutFkWjSZu.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-06-13\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":15,\"name\":\"Episode 15\",\"overview\":\"Jacqui Joseph finds a drop-leaf table, a pair of legless dining chairs and a collection of unwanted curtains at High Wycombe recycling centre for her and the team to upcycle.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/w6TePybFLjKEIZAySSDIs08gWdI.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-06-15\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":16,\"name\":\"Episode 16\",\"overview\":\"Jacqui Joseph saves a pair of worn-down wicker chairs, an old coal scuttle and a pair of bedside tables from the skips at Beaconsfield recycling centre.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/rxE1nrAOV7SKIK7YmRQum1fDRwi.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-06-19\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":17,\"name\":\"Episode 17\",\"overview\":\"Sarah Moore hopes to breathe new life into a set of dining chairs, a chipboard cabinet and a collection of vintage coat hangers.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/9U1h0tSt22RensRJg6kwde6rkAq.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-06-20\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":18,\"name\":\"Episode 18\",\"overview\":\"Jacqui Joseph finds a pair of folding chairs, an old washstand and a collection of glass bottles to repurpose at Altrincham recycling centre.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/s86XNP2OpAn1Qw5MlLXf9cPHd92.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-06-22\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":19,\"name\":\"Episode 19\",\"overview\":\"Sarah Moore, Zoe Murphy and Peter Fournel are in Surrey to work their upcycling magic on a G Plan unit, a stacking bookcase and a papasan seat.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/hunMG2fdkxKRVTDt4AjzImmCGdA.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-06-26\",\"runtime\":43},{\"number\":20,\"name\":\"Episode 20\",\"overview\":\"Jacqui Joseph saves a drop-leaf table, a collection of canvas frames and a monk's bench from being crushed at High Wycombe recycling centre in Buckinghamshire.\",\"still\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/mfUTc7DHkaKAAWTAs9jrBCyYQEU.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2023-06-28\",\"runtime\":43}],\"firstAirDate\":\"2015-09-07\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}